1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,560
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:05,270
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:06,460
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,890
I've been a nurse for
twenty-six years.

5
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:11,870
Twelve-hour shifts on hard
hospital floors,

6
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,510
on my feet all shift,

7
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:15,110
kneeling at bedsides,

8
00:00:15,110 --> 00:00:17,190
lifting and turning
patients more times

9
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:18,580
than I could ever count.

10
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,750
That's a lot of years

11
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:21,180
on a pair of knees.

12
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,140
I had my right knee

13
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,780
replaced two years ago.

14
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,590
It has hurt every day
since.

15
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:26,930
Not surgery pain.

16
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:28,090
I know what that felt
like,

17
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:28,960
and it went away.

18
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,210
This is different.

19
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:31,020
Tight.

20
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:31,920
Full.

21
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:32,810
Like a band around

22
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,600
the joint that never
loosens.

23
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,800
And for two years

24
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,410
I've been told the same
thing.

25
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:38,540
Give it time.

26
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,980
At six weeks it was
swelling,

27
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,290
and swelling is normal.

28
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,290
At three months,

29
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:43,440
give it six.

30
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:44,150
At six months,

31
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:45,770
some knees take a full
year.

32
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:46,460
At a year,

33
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,850
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

34
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:50,330
And I didn't just wait.

35
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:51,970
We went down the list.

36
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:53,360
More physical therapy.

37
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,220
Every session,

38
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,870
every exercise at home.

39
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:57,040
I got stronger.

40
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,710
The tightness never moved.

41
00:00:58,710 --> 00:01:00,030
The pain pills helped,

42
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:01,450
and that was the problem.

43
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:03,390
I'm already on enough
every morning,

44
00:01:03,390 --> 00:01:04,360
and nobody could tell me

45
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:05,890
when I'd get to stop.

46
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:07,100
Then a nerve block.

47
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,800
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

48
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:10,110
And after that, a second

49
00:01:10,110 --> 00:01:11,190
operation to go back

50
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:12,790
in and do it over.

51
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:13,900
I said no.

52
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,800
Every morning I pulled on
my scrubs

53
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:16,790
and my knee felt like

54
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:18,740
a band was wrapped around
it,

55
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:21,590
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

56
00:01:21,590 --> 00:01:22,850
Every morning I took
something

57
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:23,850
for it and went

58
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:24,950
in for my shift.

59
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:26,500
Couldn't do the stairs,

60
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,590
couldn't stand at the
counter

61
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:29,150
long enough to finish
dinner,

62
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:30,670
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

63
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:33,020
game without shifting
every two minutes.

64
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:34,500
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,860
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:38,490
like getting in the car

67
00:01:38,490 --> 00:01:40,040
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,190
into a decision.

69
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:42,490
After a long and serious

70
00:01:42,490 --> 00:01:43,790
talk with my wife,

71
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:46,010
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:47,170
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:49,050
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:49,050 --> 00:01:50,740
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:53,190
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:54,910
No loosening, no
infection,

77
00:01:54,910 --> 00:01:55,920
nothing wrong.

78
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,760
Only this time there

79
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,170
was no new number.

80
00:01:58,170 --> 00:01:59,220
Nobody said

81
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:00,490
give it another six
months.

82
00:02:00,490 --> 00:02:02,350
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:03,160
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,390
lot for a while.

85
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:05,930
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:07,500
Then explain this.

87
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,400
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,890
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:10,890 --> 00:02:13,030
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:15,230
I'd pulled a double shift
that day.

91
00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:17,040
Everyone in the house was
asleep

92
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,140
and I was downstairs in
the recliner,

93
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:20,750
still in my scrubs,

94
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:21,880
with my leg up,

95
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,390
trying to find any angle

96
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:24,820
where it didn't feel like
something

97
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:27,130
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

98
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:29,520
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

99
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,660
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

100
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:32,650
And I just thought,

101
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,410
is this really my life
now?

102
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:36,150
I can't live like this.

103
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:38,050
So I made myself a
promise.

104
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:38,900
I wouldn't go a day

105
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,700
without looking for an
answer.

106
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:42,280
And when I found one,

107
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,160
I'd share it with everyone

108
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,040
going through the same
thing.

109
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,150
So I got my laptop

110
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:49,050
out and went looking.

111
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:50,420
Not for a product.

112
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,930
For an explanation.

113
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:53,590
Mayo Clinic forums,

114
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:55,720
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

115
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,360
doctor videos, medical
animations.

116
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,290
And that's when I found

117
00:02:59,290 --> 00:03:01,080
a video from a physical
therapist

118
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:01,610
named Dr.

119
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:03,620
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

120
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,570
had been through exactly
this.

121
00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:07,820
But before I say anything
else,

122
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:09,630
I want to be straight with
you.

123
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:12,020
You've already had
something work fast.

124
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:12,960
The ice.

125
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,590
The first week of a new
pill.

126
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:16,510
The good day after a
session.

127
00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:17,610
Then it wore off.

128
00:03:17,610 --> 00:03:20,170
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

129
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:22,300
Fast relief isn't relief.

130
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,590
It's a preview.

131
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:24,610
So I'm not going to tell

132
00:03:24,610 --> 00:03:26,060
you this works fast.

133
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:27,230
It doesn't.

134
00:03:27,230 --> 00:03:29,100
But if you're willing to
be patient,

135
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:29,820
and to look at what's

136
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,110
going on around your new
knee

137
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:32,710
instead of inside it,
there

138
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:34,910
is a real reason it still
hurts.

139
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:37,230
And something you can do
about it.

140
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:38,530
Let me explain what he
said,

141
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:39,950
because this is what
changed

142
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:41,400
everything for me.

143
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:43,480
He started with the
basics.

144
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,980
A knee replacement takes
out

145
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:46,720
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

146
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,130
in metal and plastic.

147
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:50,140
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

148
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,950
you had before the
operation.

149
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:53,610
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:54,950
But then he explained
something

151
00:03:54,950 --> 00:03:56,320
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,140
He said,

153
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:58,820
think about a swollen foot

154
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:00,510
inside a shoe.

155
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:01,920
The shoe didn't shrink.

156
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:04,120
Your foot is taking up
more room,

157
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,550
so everything feels
cramped

158
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:07,160
and tight and squeezed.

159
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,030
Your new knee sits

160
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:09,540
in a limited space with
living

161
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,570
tissue packed all around
it.

162
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:13,430
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

163
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:15,260
had to work through that
tissue.

164
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:18,140
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

165
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,670
At first that's normal.

166
00:04:19,670 --> 00:04:21,280
But in some people that
swelling can

167
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:24,050
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

168
00:04:24,050 --> 00:04:25,910
And swollen tissue takes
up more

169
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:27,860
room than calm tissue
does.

170
00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:29,220
So when you bend,

171
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,090
that tissue gets
compressed.

172
00:04:31,090 --> 00:04:32,310
When you straighten,

173
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:33,880
it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,070
That's the band.

175
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:37,490
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

176
00:04:37,490 --> 00:04:38,450
And you start being

177
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:39,560
the one who says,

178
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,430
you go ahead.

179
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:41,800
I'll stay here.

180
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,620
And that's exactly why so
much

181
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:46,010
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

182
00:04:46,010 --> 00:04:48,150
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

183
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:49,200
around the knee.

184
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,200
Worth doing,

185
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,190
and I'd done it.

186
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:52,550
It does nothing about
tissue

187
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:53,840
taking up room.

188
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,330
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:57,810
the nerve carrying the
signal.

190
00:04:57,810 --> 00:04:59,910
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

191
00:04:59,910 --> 00:05:01,530
But when that irritated
tissue

192
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:03,140
finally calms down,

193
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,590
it holds less fluid,

194
00:05:04,590 --> 00:05:06,240
and it takes up less room.

195
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,580
Less room taken up means

196
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:09,720
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

197
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,890
That's what takes the
pressure off.

198
00:05:11,890 --> 00:05:13,390
After two years of this,

199
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:15,330
it finally made sense.

200
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,510
The problem was never the
new knee.

201
00:05:17,510 --> 00:05:19,520
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

202
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:21,190
He calls it the squeeze.

203
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,780
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

204
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:24,840
I'd bought knee sleeves,

205
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,620
compression braces,
creams,

206
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,140
half of Amazon really,

207
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:29,930
and all any of it gave me

208
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:30,860
was an hour.

209
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:31,780
I even looked at going

210
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,820
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

211
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,570
But at $200 a session

212
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:37,900
with nothing covered by
insurance,

213
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,520
that was a quick no.

214
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:40,600
Then one night I went

215
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,970
back to that knee
replacement

216
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:43,920
group and actually read
it.

217
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,270
Thousands of people,

218
00:05:45,270 --> 00:05:47,030
years out from surgery,

219
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:49,620
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

220
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,320
nobody could explain.

221
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:53,240
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

222
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:55,220
the same thing kept coming
up.

223
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:56,650
This one device,

224
00:05:56,650 --> 00:05:59,120
and people saying it was
the first

225
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,510
thing that made a
difference.

226
00:06:00,510 --> 00:06:02,510
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

227
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:03,860
alright, here it comes,

228
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,320
he's selling me something,

229
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:07,220
let me shut that down
right now.

230
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,090
I'm only here because I
made myself

231
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:11,470
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

232
00:06:11,470 --> 00:06:12,490
that if I ever found

233
00:06:12,490 --> 00:06:13,880
something that helped,

234
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:15,220
I'd say so.

235
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:16,910
It's called the KenRelief
Red

236
00:06:16,910 --> 00:06:18,580
Light Therapy Wrap.

237
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:21,050
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

238
00:06:21,050 --> 00:06:22,380
It looked like the cheap

239
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:25,000
knee sleeves off Amazon

240
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,880
that did nothing for me.

241
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,180
But I went to their
website anyway,

242
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,340
just to see what all

243
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:31,920
the fuss was about.

244
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,740
It's the same red light
therapy

245
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:36,790
clinics charge $200 a
session

246
00:06:36,790 --> 00:06:39,010
for, off machines that
cost

247
00:06:39,010 --> 00:06:40,790
fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:40,790 --> 00:06:42,120
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,920
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,950
Two hundred and forty
lights.

251
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:48,250
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:50,810
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:53,380
run together for the
strongest effect.

254
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:55,180
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:57,450
A five to thirty minute
timer.

256
00:06:57,450 --> 00:06:59,270
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:00,790
Ninety days.

258
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:02,490
Results or your money
back,

259
00:07:02,490 --> 00:07:04,810
no questions, no store
credit,

260
00:07:04,810 --> 00:07:06,930
and you don't even send it
back.

261
00:07:06,930 --> 00:07:09,280
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

262
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,240
days to change my mind.

263
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,410
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:12,410 --> 00:07:13,430
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:14,860
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:17,100
Only the right knee was
replaced,

267
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,160
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

268
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:21,620
and I'd done it for two
years.

269
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:23,670
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:23,670 --> 00:07:24,270
When it came,

271
00:07:24,270 --> 00:07:26,440
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,640
because I'd been let down
too

273
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,510
many times to get excited.

274
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:31,100
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:33,150
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:34,980
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:37,400
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,470
And that was it.

279
00:07:38,470 --> 00:07:40,150
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:40,150 --> 00:07:41,380
When I took it off,

281
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,270
I'll be honest,

282
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:44,180
nothing dramatic had
happened.

283
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:45,800
And after what that video
said,

284
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,980
that's exactly what I
expected.

285
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:48,720
What was different

286
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:49,690
was that for the first

287
00:07:49,690 --> 00:07:50,780
time in two years

288
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:52,120
I'd done something for my
knee

289
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,610
instead of to it.

290
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:54,640
Twenty minutes,

291
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,840
in my own chair.

292
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,870
No drive, no copay.

293
00:07:57,870 --> 00:08:00,110
They say twenty minutes.

294
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:01,190
I did thirty,

295
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,470
twice a day,

296
00:08:02,470 --> 00:08:04,660
lowest setting that first
week.

297
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,150
I put it on the calendar.

298
00:08:06,150 --> 00:08:06,850
The first week,

299
00:08:06,850 --> 00:08:07,700
I couldn't have told

300
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,540
you if anything was
happening.

301
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:10,410
I tried not to get

302
00:08:10,410 --> 00:08:11,110
my hopes up.

303
00:08:11,110 --> 00:08:12,500
I'd had things help for a
week

304
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,590
and then stop.

305
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:14,850
But somewhere in the
second week

306
00:08:14,850 --> 00:08:15,920
I noticed I'd come down

307
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,840
the stairs without holding
the rail.

308
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,310
I hadn't decided to.

309
00:08:19,310 --> 00:08:20,310
I just did it,

310
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:21,970
then stopped halfway down

311
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:23,450
because I realized.

312
00:08:23,450 --> 00:08:25,050
By the end of the fourth
week

313
00:08:25,050 --> 00:08:26,150
I'd slept through the
night

314
00:08:26,150 --> 00:08:27,630
four times running.

315
00:08:27,630 --> 00:08:28,980
I stood at the counter

316
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:30,210
and finished making dinner

317
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:32,160
without looking for the
stool.

318
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:33,790
None of that is dramatic.

319
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:34,740
All of it was gone

320
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:36,080
for two years.

321
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,700
A few weeks later my wife
asked

322
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:38,650
if I wanted to walk

323
00:08:38,650 --> 00:08:40,810
the long way around the
block.

324
00:08:40,810 --> 00:08:41,890
And for the first time

325
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:42,700
in two years,

326
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:44,020
I said yes.

327
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,890
I wanted to understand
why,

328
00:08:45,890 --> 00:08:47,550
so I read the whole thing.

329
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:49,290
It comes down to four
steps.

330
00:08:49,290 --> 00:08:50,250
One.

331
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:52,000
The tissue around a new
knee can

332
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,270
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

333
00:08:55,270 --> 00:08:56,190
Two.

334
00:08:56,190 --> 00:08:58,720
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

335
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,760
so it takes up more

336
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,220
room than it should.

337
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,160
Three.

338
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,840
There's only so much room
in there.

339
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,670
Bending compresses it.

340
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:07,380
Straightening pulls it
tight.

341
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,920
That's the squeeze.

342
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:09,970
Four.

343
00:09:09,970 --> 00:09:12,270
Red and near-infrared
light have been

344
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:14,480
studied for calming that
inflammation,

345
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,820
so the swelling and the
pressure

346
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:17,270
can come down with it.

347
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:18,260
In a randomized trial,

348
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,830
patients given light
therapy after

349
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:20,610
a knee replacement

350
00:09:20,610 --> 00:09:21,360
had less pain,

351
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,320
less swelling

352
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:23,910
and better early movement
than

353
00:09:23,910 --> 00:09:25,160
those who weren't.

354
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,620
A 2025 review said the
same,

355
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,780
and was clear the evidence

356
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:29,900
is still limited.

357
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,090
I probably sound like a
broken record

358
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:33,660
to the people I work with.

359
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,590
But after two years of
doing everything

360
00:09:35,590 --> 00:09:37,460
I was told and getting
nowhere,

361
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:38,790
you have no idea what it's

362
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,380
like to sleep through the
night,

363
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:41,640
say yes to the walk,

364
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,330
and get my life back.

365
00:09:43,330 --> 00:09:44,700
So take it from me.

366
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,040
Don't spend another year
waiting

367
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,220
for it to settle.

368
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:49,190
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

369
00:09:49,190 --> 00:09:50,560
More than ten thousand
people

370
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,700
with pain after a knee

371
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:54,600
replacement have already
tried this.

372
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,450
Some had it worse than I
did.

373
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:57,590
You can get the KenRelief

374
00:09:57,590 --> 00:09:59,170
